Install dotenv from PowerShell

cd F:\OpenHack\network_scan_react\backend

python -m pip install python-dotenv

===========================================================================

Open the official Groq API Keys page:

GroqCloud API Keys >> https://console.groq.com/keys?utm_source=chatgpt.com

Create the key

Give it a name >> Network Monitoring Dash

Then create the key >> gsk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

Create this file: F:\OpenHack\network_scan_react\backend\.env

Inside .env, put:	GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_ABC123........

Do not put quotes around it.

This will be used by >> ai_engine.py

===========================================================================

On PowerShell >> 
python -c "from dotenv import load_dotenv; import os; load_dotenv(); print('GROQ_API_KEY loaded:', bool(os.getenv('GROQ_API_KEY')))"

>> GROQ_API_KEY loaded: True